    },
    {
      "text": "Pangea Design",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "-1",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "**Variable Angle Locking Technology**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "Pangea’s variable angle locking technology uses a CoCr locking screw, which is harder than the Ti6Al4V ELI plate, allowing for the screwhead’s threads to form a definitive locking position in the plate’s locking hole by engaging the softer, Ti6Al4V ELI material.",
              "table": null,
              "images": [
                {
                  "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/423214/images/eac996da-d99c-4b39-bc30-4c584b37dbda_screenshot_2025-01-14_at_3.18.48_pm.jpg",
                  "caption": ""
                }
              ],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "This technology allows the user to aim and lock the screw into the plate within a true 30° cone of the predetermined hole trajectory. The variable angle drill guide provided with the system offers guidance with respect to the limit of the 30° cone. The locking mechanism remains functional for up to three attempts at locking screw insertion.",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "Circular universal holes accept nonlocking screws, and locking screws within a 30° cone",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "**Posterolateral Extension**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "Asymmetric plate shape designed to support posterior buttressing by extending the plate more laterally",
              "table": null,
              "images": [
                {
                  "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/423214/images/3516d790-a3ef-491d-b6cf-78b8ba2b989a_screenshot_2025-01-14_at_3.19.11_pm.jpg",
                  "caption": ""
                }
              ],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "**Posteromedial Extension Hole**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "Allows buttress effect while facilitating lateral capture of the medial fragment",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "**Proximal Rafting Screws**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "Designed with variable angle locking technology which allows improved placement in conjunction with lateral based implant",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "**Oblong Hole**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "To aid in plate placement",
              "table": null,
              "images": [
                {
                  "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/423214/images/1f4a91df-bbdd-4323-9fbe-925e4ccd354b_screenshot_2025-01-14_at_3.15.52_pm.jpg",
                  "caption": ""
                }
              ],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "**2.0mm K-Wire Hole Distally**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Placement",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "-1",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "This plate is designed to be used for a medial coronal shear fracture of a Schatzker VI",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Plate position as well as screw options facilitate the use with Pangea proximal lateral tibia plates.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "This plate sits on the posterior medial side and wraps around posteriorly",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Fit",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "-1",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Proximal Posteromedial Tibia Plate is designed to address both partial articular medial plateau fractures as well as support medial fracture fragments associated with bicondylar fractures",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "The posterorlateral extension is designed to support more lateral posterior buttressing",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Designed with the use of SOMA: Stryker Orthopedics Modeling and Analytics",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "The Pangea Proximal Posteromedial Tibia Plates provide better anatomic fit compared to competitive Synthes LCP Medial Proximal Tibia Plates. 2",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Indications",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "-1",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "The Pangea Tibia Plating System is indicated for the internal fixation and stabilization of tibia bone fractures and osteotomies in normal and osteopenic bone, including:",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "Diaphyseal, metaphyseal, epiphyseal, extra- and intra-articular fractures",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "Non-unions, malunions, and deformities",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "Periprosthetic fractures",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Approaches",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "-1",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Surgeons may use a standard medial or posteromedial approach to the proximal medial tibia.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
